@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# R49 / 0.1.36 — AirPlay receiver identity boundary hardening
+
+## Baseline
+
+- R48 / 0.1.35 candidate source.
+- R44 verified source lineage remains unchanged; R48 changes are inherited.
+- This is a security/robustness candidate. It is **not** an E2LB Bluetooth/iAP2 connection fix.
+
+## Findings addressed
+
+1. Pair-Verify M2 identity mismatch was previously thrown as generic `IOException`. `AirPlayClient` could therefore retry the same untrusted receiver response inside the pairing window. It is now `UntrustedReceiverIdentityException`, which follows the existing fail-closed stop path.
+2. Missing Pair-Verify M2 ephemeral key, encrypted identity envelope, identifier, or signature was previously treated as generic protocol I/O failure. These incomplete identity proofs now fail closed as untrusted identity.
+3. Pair-Verify ephemeral X25519 key length is checked before use; X25519 errors and all-zero shared secrets are rejected before deriving the encryption key.
+4. Pair-Setup M6 and Pair-Verify M2 receiver identifiers now require bounded (1..255 byte), strict UTF-8, nonblank text without Unicode control characters.
+5. Pair-Setup logs no longer emit the raw receiver identifier. A short SHA-256 fingerprint is used instead, avoiding control-character log injection and reducing identifier disclosure.
+6. A remembered receiver identity mismatch now has an integration regression proving it does not delete saved trust, reconnect, or fall back to a new Pair-Setup registration.
+
+## Tests
+
+Executed with Kotlin/JVM 1.9.0, JDK 21, Bouncy Castle 1.80 and the repository's focused JUnit-compatible harness:
+
+- `AirPlayPairingTest`: 28 passed.
+- `PairingRejectionTest`: 7 passed.
+- `ReconnectAttemptPolicyTest`: 4 passed (R48 class retained unchanged).
+- Total: **39 passed, 0 failed**.
+
+New fault cases include missing M2 identity fields, short and low-order X25519 ephemeral keys, malformed/empty/oversized identifiers, invalid UTF-8, control-character log injection, short signatures, and remembered-identity mismatch with no retry/fallback.
+
+`git diff --check` passed. The changed pairing production sources and focused tests compiled with `kotlinc`; the only warnings were the existing deprecated `AESEngine()` constructor and an existing unnecessary `!!` in a test.
+
+## Not verified
+
+- Full Android Gradle build, Android Lint, Spotless, APK assembly/signing and emulator tests were not run. `bash gradlew :app:testStandardDebugUnitTest --no-daemon` stopped before Gradle startup because `services.gradle.org` DNS resolution failed (`UnknownHostException`).
+- No physical E2LB test was run.
+- MFi certificate-chain/challenge signature verification is still not implemented. An observed 0xAA03 remains `RESPONSE_UNVERIFIED`; the compatibility 0xAA05 signal is not proof of authentication.
+- 0x4300 no-ACK and the receiver's new-SYN behavior remain unresolved. No protocol payload, challenge length, DUAL_GROUP/SINGLE_GROUP choice or DETECT/SYN behavior was changed without a valid native trace/specification.
+- No APK was produced and no GitHub branch or release was modified.
+
+## Acceptance status
+
+R49 improves AirPlay receiver identity failure handling and diagnostic privacy. It does not close the original Bluetooth/iAP2 startup failure. Release remains blocked on full Android CI and repeated E2LB vehicle acceptance (valid MFi evidence, 0x4300/0x4301, Wi-Fi handoff, AirPlay SETUP/RECORD, video/audio/touch, and reconnect).
